## Context

This project started as an internship system analysis and design assignment for PT Tarindo, a manufacturer of brass and PVC faucets under the AMICO brand. The scope covered inventory workflows across three production branches spanning raw material, work-in-progress (WIP), and finished goods warehouses.

## Problem

Operational records across the three branches relied on manual tracking and fragmented reporting. As a result, administration and purchasing teams faced frequent stock mismatches between physical inventory and administrative records, delayed reporting cycles, and limited real-time stock visibility.

## My role

Owner: I analyzed the warehouse-to-purchasing data flow across the three branches, identified the root causes of stock mismatches and late reporting, designed the centralized inventory workflow, and implemented the Django web prototype.

## As-is analysis

Mapping the existing workflow across raw material, WIP, and finished goods storage showed that stock updates were recorded locally and reconciled manually afterward. That lag made cross-branch coordination difficult and prevented administrative staff from seeing accurate stock positions when planning purchases.

## Requirements

- Centralized browser-based inventory records accessible across production branches.
- Role-aware user authentication and structured access for administrative and warehouse staff.
- Clear tracking of stock-in, stock-out, and item balances across raw materials, WIP, and finished goods.
- Faster, more consistent reporting to align physical stock with administrative records.

## Solution design

The prototype was developed using Rapid Application Development (RAD) so stakeholders could review working screens early and validate workflow fit before full rollout. Django's modular app structure (`Inventory_Project`, `SI`, and `users`) separated user management from inventory operations while keeping data models consistent.

## Build

Built with Python, Django, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and containerized with Docker for live demo deployment on Vercel (`inventory-demo-woad.vercel.app`). Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Informasi-Manajemen-Inventory](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Informasi-Manajemen-Inventory).

## Verification

Validated the end-to-end prototype flows (user login, item record entry, and stock movement updates) in the deployed web environment and documented the analysis and design in an academic journal paper.

## Outcome

Delivered a working centralized inventory web prototype that addressed cross-branch stock visibility gaps, and published the study in Diponegoro University's E-Journal (June 2025).

## Reflection

Starting with the physical warehouse-to-purchasing data flow before writing code ensured the prototype targeted the real causes of stock discrepancies rather than simply digitizing broken spreadsheets.
